Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 23:46:16 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 29/34] WP16: Separate data-encryption key and more encrypted
 fields

Integration: ADDED_COLUMNS conflict in db.py (WP15, WP12) kept all columns; the secret-handling section kept WP22's audit_retention above it. main.py conflict with WP06/WP08: kept WP06's role check and startup_lock block and WP08's image bound, and call db.check_data_keys() inside the lock right after config.secret_key(). app/worker.py (WP06) now calls db.check_data_keys() at start too, so a bad key also stops the worker. Cross-WP fix: tests/test_retention_alignment.py (WP22) read SELECT request_xml directly; with request_xml now encrypted it reads the decrypted value through SELECT *.

Added test_the_worker_refuses_to_start_with_a_malformed_data_key to tests/test_worker.py.
